        "Hastelloy C22":
          "Offers better overall corrosion resistance than C276 in oxidizing environments. Provides superior protection against weld-zone attack and pitting.",
        "Hastelloy C2000":
          "Specifically designed for maximum flexibility with added copper. Excels in sulfuric acid and provides broader resistance to a variety of mixed process streams.",
        "Hastelloy C4 & C59":
          "C4 offers high-temperature stability and resistance to grain-boundary precipitation. C59 is a high-purity alloy with excellent thermal stability and resistance to pitting in halide media.",
        "Hastelloy B2":
          "A nickel-molybdenum alloy with significant resistance to reducing environments. A primary choice for handling pure hydrochloric, phosphoric, and sulfuric acids.",
        "Hastelloy B3":
          "An improved version of B2, offering the same high resistance to hydrochloric acid but with significantly better thermal stability for easier fabrication and welding.",
        "Hastelloy HN":
          "Also known as Alloy N (UNS N10003), developed specifically for molten fluoride salts. Has excellent oxidation resistance to hot fluoride salts at temperatures up to 704°C (1300°F).",
