  shortDescription: "Premium high-performance alloy round bars including Nimonic 75/80A, Nichrome 80/20, Nitronic 50 (XM-19), Nilo 36/42, and Alloy 286/926. Engineered for mission-critical applications requiring ultra-high temperature creep resistance, corrosion resistance, or controlled thermal expansion. Manufactured to ASTM B637, B446, A276, B160 and AMS 5662, 5581, 5666 standards.",
  
  technicalOverview: "This selection of specialized alloy round bars is engineered for mission-critical industrial applications where standard materials fail due to thermal fatigue, extreme mechanical stress, or aggressive chemical attack. These bars provide unique solutions ranging from ultra-high temperature creep resistance to controlled thermal expansion for precision engineering. Nimonic alloys are nickel-chromium-based superalloys designed for high-temperature service where creep resistance and oxidation stability are primary concerns. Nimonic 75 (UNS N06075) offers excellent oxidation resistance and mechanical properties at high temperatures, widely used for structural components in high-heat zones and furnace internals. Nimonic 80A (UNS N07080) is a precipitation-hardenable alloy strengthened by aluminum and titanium, providing significantly higher creep-rupture properties for service up to 815°C (1500°F). Nichrome 80/20 (80% Nickel, 20% Chromium) in round bar form serves as a robust heat-resistant material, forming a stable layer of chromium oxide that protects against degradation during repeated thermal cycling. Nitronic 50 (UNS S20910) is a nitrogen-strengthened austenitic stainless steel providing superior corrosion resistance and yield strength compared to Types 316 and 317, remaining non-magnetic even after severe cold working. The Nilo series (Invar family) is engineered for applications requiring dimensional stability across varying temperatures. Nilo 42 (UNS K94100) features a low coefficient of thermal expansion up to 300°C (570°F), specifically designed for glass-to-metal and ceramic-to-metal seals. Nilo 48 (UNS K94800) matches the thermal expansion of specific soft glasses and ceramics. Alloy 286 (UNS S66000) is an iron-base, age-hardenable superalloy designed for high strength and corrosion resistance up to 700°C (1290°F). Alloy 926 (UNS N08926) is a super-austenitic 6% Molybdenum stainless steel providing exceptional resistance to pitting and crevice corrosion in high-chloride media like seawater and acidic bleach.",

