  shortDescription: "Premium Monel 400 (UNS N04400), K500 (UNS N05500), and R405 (UNS N04405) nickel-copper alloy round bars engineered for exceptional corrosion resistance in marine environments, hydrofluoric acid service, and high-strength applications. Manufactured to ASTM B164, B564, B865 and ASME SB164, SB564, SB865 standards.",
  
  technicalOverview: "Monel 400 is a solid-solution alloy that can only be hardened by cold working, containing approximately 63% nickel and 30% copper. It offers exceptional resistance to rapidly flowing seawater and brackish water, and is one of the few materials that can handle hydrofluoric acid (HF) in all concentrations up to the boiling point. It maintains excellent mechanical properties at sub-zero temperatures and does not undergo a ductile-to-brittle transition even at the temperature of liquid hydrogen. Monel K500 combines the excellent corrosion resistance of Monel 400 with the added advantages of greater strength and hardness through the addition of aluminum and titanium for precipitation hardening. It offers approximately three times the yield strength of Monel 400 and remains non-magnetic even at very low temperatures. It provides superior resistance to spark generation and is highly resistant to sour-gas environments. Monel R405 is the free-machining version of Monel 400 with a controlled amount of sulfur added to provide sulfide inclusions that act as chip breakers during machining operations. It is designed specifically for use with automatic screw machines, possessing the same corrosion resistance and physical properties as Monel 400 but with significantly improved cutting speeds.",

