      "Inconel 601": "UNS N06601 (2.4851) – Features additional aluminum content providing enhanced resistance to high-temperature oxidation and spalling, even under severely cyclic heating conditions.",
      "Inconel 625": "UNS N06625 (2.4856) – Derives high strength and fatigue resistance from molybdenum and niobium addition. Highly resistant to pitting and crevice corrosion in seawater and chloride-heavy process streams.",
      "Inconel 690": "UNS N06690 (2.4642) – Engineered with high chromium content for excellent resistance to oxidizing acids and salts. Primary choice for nuclear steam generator components and high-temperature furnace internals.",
      "Inconel 718": "UNS N07718 (2.4668) – High-strength, corrosion-resistant alloy used from -253°C to 704°C. Renowned for excellent weldability and resistance to post-weld cracking, essential for gas turbine blades and rocket motors.",
      "Inconel 725": "UNS N07725 – Age-hardenable version of Alloy 625 providing nearly double the mechanical strength of annealed 625 grade while maintaining similar corrosion resistance. Ideal for high-strength fasteners in sour gas environments.",
      "Inconel X-750": "UNS N07750 (2.4669) – Optimized for high-temperature structural components requiring minimal relaxation and high creep-rupture strength under heavy loads. Commonly used for springs and bolts in high-heat environments."
