  technicalOverview: "Hastelloy C-Series is the most versatile group of Hastelloy alloys, designed to handle a broad spectrum of volatile chemical process streams. Hastelloy C276 (UNS N10276) is the industry standard for aggressive environments, exceptionally resistant to wet chlorine gas, hypochlorites, and chlorine dioxide. Hastelloy C22 (UNS N06022) offers better overall corrosion resistance than C276 in oxidizing environments with superior protection against localized corrosion, frequently used in pharmaceutical and biotech valve fabrication. Hastelloy C2000 (UNS N06200) is a unique alloy with deliberate copper additions, providing maximum versatility in both oxidizing and reducing environments, excelling specifically in sulfuric acid service. Hastelloy C59, C4, and C-4 are specialized grades optimized for thermal stability and resistance to grain-boundary precipitation. The B-series alloys are specifically engineered for resistance against reducing environments, particularly hydrochloric acid (HCl). Hastelloy B2 (UNS N10665) is a nickel-molybdenum alloy with significant resistance to hydrochloric acid at all concentrations and temperatures. Hastelloy B3 (UNS N10675) is an improved version of B2 with significantly enhanced thermal stability, making fabrication and machining of heavy bars easier while maintaining the same high level of resistance to reducing acids.",

