      "Duplex S31803": "UNS S31803 (1.4462 / F51 / 2205) – Widely used duplex grade. Exceptional resistance to pitting and crevice corrosion in chloride-bearing environments. Highly resistant to stress corrosion cracking (SCC) in temperatures up to 150°C.",
      "Duplex S32205": "UNS S32205 (1.4462 / F60 / 2205) – Nitrogen-enhanced version of S31803. Dual certified with S31803, offering improved mechanical properties and corrosion resistance. PREN > 34.",
      "Super Duplex S32750": "UNS S32750 (1.4410 / F53 / 2507) – Highly alloyed grade with 25% Chromium and 4% Molybdenum. PREN > 40. Designed for high-strength applications in extremely corrosive conditions such as warm seawater.",
      "Super Duplex S32760": "UNS S32760 (1.4501 / F55 / Zeron 100) – Includes deliberate additions of Copper and Tungsten for enhanced resistance to mineral acids like sulfuric and hydrochloric acid in contaminated media.",
      "Super Duplex S32550": "UNS S32550 (1.4507 / F61 / Ferralium 255) – High-copper super duplex grade offering superior erosion-corrosion resistance and high hardness. Ideal for rotating parts in abrasive slurries."
