  shortDescription: "Premium Stainless Steel sheets in grades 304/304L, 316/316L, 310S, 321, 317L, 904L, 17-4 PH, 253 MA, and more. Engineered for diverse applications from food processing to high-temperature heat exchangers. Manufactured to ASTM A240, ASME SA240, ASTM A666, and EN 10088-2 standards.",
  
  technicalOverview: "Stainless steel sheets are a fundamental component in industrial fabrication, offering a versatile range of corrosion resistance, aesthetic finishes, and mechanical properties. These austenitic and martensitic grades are engineered to perform across a wide thermal spectrum, from cryogenic storage to high-heat furnace environments. Unlike thicker plates, sheets are prioritized for their surface quality, formability, and precision thickness. SS 304/304L (UNS S30400/S30403) is the global standard for general-purpose applications, ideal for food processing, kitchenware, and architectural panels. SS 316/316L (UNS S31600/S31603) is infused with Molybdenum to combat chloride-induced pitting, making it the primary choice for pharmaceutical equipment, chemical containers, and coastal architectural projects. SS 309 & 310S are high-alloy grades designed for oxidation resistance, with 310S (UNS S31008) specifically utilized for continuous service up to 1100°C. SS 321 (UNS S32100) is Titanium-stabilized to eliminate intergranular corrosion in the 'sensitization' temperature range (427°C to 815°C). 253 MA (UNS S30815) is a high-performance lean austenitic grade that uses rare earth metals and nitrogen to provide superior creep strength and oxidation resistance up to 1150°C.",

