  title: "High-Performance Alloy Sheets – Nimonic, Nichrome, Nitronic, Nilo & Alloy",
  shortDescription: "Premium high-performance alloy sheets including Nimonic 75/80A, Nichrome 80/20, Nitronic 50 (XM-19), Nilo 42/48, Alloy 286 (660), and Alloy 926 (6Mo). Engineered for mission-critical applications requiring ultra-high temperature creep resistance, corrosion resistance, or controlled thermal expansion. Manufactured to ASTM B168, B443, B670, AMS 5596, and AMS 5542 standards.",
  
  technicalOverview: "Nimonic alloys are nickel-chromium-based superalloys designed for high-temperature service where creep resistance and oxidation stability are primary concerns. Nimonic 75 (UNS N06075) offers excellent oxidation resistance and mechanical properties at high temperatures, widely used for high-temperature structural components and furnace liners. Nimonic 80A (UNS N07080) is a precipitation-hardenable alloy strengthened by aluminum and titanium, providing significantly higher creep-rupture properties for service up to 815°C (1500°F). Nichrome 80/20 (80% Nickel, 20% Chromium) in sheet form serves as a robust heat-resistant material, forming a stable layer of chromium oxide that protects against degradation during repeated thermal cycling. Nitronic 50 (UNS S20910) is a nitrogen-strengthened austenitic stainless steel providing superior corrosion resistance and yield strength compared to Types 316 and 317, remaining non-magnetic even after severe cold working. The Nilo series (Invar family) is engineered for applications requiring dimensional stability across varying temperatures. Nilo 42 (UNS K94100) features a low coefficient of thermal expansion up to 300°C (570°F), specifically designed for glass-to-metal and ceramic-to-metal seals. Nilo 48 (UNS K94800) matches the thermal expansion of specific soft glasses and ceramics. Alloy 286 (UNS S66000) is an iron-base, age-hardenable superalloy designed for high strength and corrosion resistance up to 700°C (1290°F). Alloy 926 (UNS N08926) is a super-austenitic 6% Molybdenum stainless steel providing exceptional resistance to pitting and crevice corrosion in high-chloride media like seawater and acidic bleach.",

  materialGroup: "High-Performance Nickel & Superalloys",
