  shortDescription: "Premium Nickel Alloy 200 (UNS N02200) and 201 (UNS N02201) commercially pure wrought nickel sheets engineered for exceptional resistance to caustic alkalis, high thermal and electrical conductivity, and purity maintenance in sensitive process flows. Manufactured to ASTM B162, ASME SB162, DIN 17750, and BS 3072 standards.",
  
  technicalOverview: "Nickel Alloy 200 (UNS N02200) and its low-carbon variant, Nickel Alloy 201 (UNS N02201), are commercially pure wrought nickel sheets. These materials are highly valued in technical industries for their unique combination of high electrical and thermal conductivity, excellent mechanical properties, and extraordinary resistance to a wide range of corrosive environments. While Nickel 200 is the standard grade for most applications, Nickel 201 is specifically engineered for service at temperatures exceeding 315°C (600°F). The lower carbon content in the 201 grade prevents embrittlement caused by intergranular carbon precipitation at high temperatures, ensuring structural integrity in high-heat environments. These sheets offer the highest resistance of any metallic material to caustic alkalis, particularly sodium hydroxide (caustic soda), at all concentrations and temperatures up to and including the molten state. They possess significantly higher thermal and electrical conductivity than stainless steels and most nickel-base superalloys, making them ideal for heat transfer and precision electronic components. As commercially pure materials, they do not introduce metallic contamination into sensitive process flows, which is critical for food, fiber, and pharmaceutical production. Nickel 200/201 sheets are ferromagnetic at room temperature, with high Curie temperatures and strong magnetostrictive properties.",

