  shortDescription: "Premium Monel 400 (UNS N04400 / 2.4360) nickel-copper alloy sheets engineered for exceptional resistance to seawater, hydrofluoric acid, and a vast array of corrosive chemicals. Ideal for marine engineering, chemical processing, and hydrofluoric acid service. Manufactured to ASTM B127, ASME SB127, BS 3072, and QQ-N-281 standards.",
  
  technicalOverview: "Monel 400 sheets (UNS N04400) are high-performance nickel-copper alloy products renowned for their exceptional resistance to seawater and a vast array of corrosive chemicals. This solid-solution alloy is characterized by high strength and toughness across a broad temperature range, from cryogenic levels up to 538°C (1000°F). Because it can only be hardened by cold working, Monel 400 sheets offer excellent ductility and weldability, making them a staple in marine engineering and chemical processing. The alloy's unique composition—approximately 63% Nickel and 30% Copper—creates a versatile material that resists both oxidizing and reducing environments better than commercially pure nickel or copper alone. Monel 400 is the industry standard for marine applications, providing outstanding resistance to rapidly flowing seawater and virtual immunity to chloride-ion stress corrosion cracking. It is one of the few metallic materials capable of handling all concentrations of hydrofluoric acid (HF) up to the boiling point, and performs excellently in deaerated hydrochloric and sulfuric acids under reducing conditions. It is also highly resistant to all forms of alkalis, including caustic soda, making it ideal for the pulp and paper and soap industries.",

