  shortDescription: "Premium Incoloy sheets in grades 800, 800H, 800HT, 825, 925, and 330 (DS 330). Nickel-iron-chromium superalloys engineered for high-temperature strength and corrosion resistance, offering excellent oxidation resistance and structural stability. Manufactured to ASTM B409, B424, B625 and ASME SB409, SB424 standards.",
  
  technicalOverview: "Incoloy sheets are nickel-iron-chromium superalloys engineered to provide a high-performance, cost-effective solution for environments requiring both high-temperature strength and resistance to various forms of corrosion. These alloys act as a bridge between standard stainless steels and high-nickel superalloys, offering excellent oxidation resistance and structural stability. By balancing nickel and iron content, Incoloy sheets maintain their mechanical properties under prolonged thermal stress and aggressive chemical exposure. The 800 Series is the industry standard for high-temperature structural applications requiring creep and rupture strength. Incoloy 800 (UNS N08800) is the base grade used for general heat-resistant applications, offering excellent resistance to oxidation and carburization at temperatures up to 593°C (1100°F). Incoloy 800H / 800HT (UNS N08810 / N08811) offer significantly higher creep-rupture properties for service above 593°C. Incoloy DS (and its close relative Alloy 330) are specialized for the heat-treating industry with increased silicon content for superior resistance to 'green rot' and internal oxidation. Incoloy 825 (UNS N08825) is a titanium-stabilized alloy with added molybdenum and copper, providing exceptional resistance to many corrosive environments, particularly sulfuric and phosphoric acids. Incoloy 925 (UNS N09925) is an age-hardenable version of Alloy 825 providing the same superior corrosion resistance but with much higher mechanical strength and hardness through precipitation hardening.",

  materialGroup: "Nickel-Iron-Chromium Superalloys",
  standards: "ASTM B409, B424, B625 / ASME SB409, SB424",
