  shortDescription: "Premium Hastelloy sheets in grades C276, C22, B2, B3, C2000, C59, C4, and HN. High-performance nickel-molybdenum-chromium superalloys engineered to withstand the most aggressive chemical environments, offering exceptional resistance to pitting, stress-corrosion cracking, and a wide range of volatile chemical media. Manufactured to ASTM B333, B575 and ASME SB333, SB575 standards.",
  
  technicalOverview: "Hastelloy sheets are high-performance nickel-molybdenum-chromium superalloys engineered to withstand the most aggressive chemical environments. These sheets maintain exceptional mechanical integrity and corrosion resistance where standard stainless steels fail. Hastelloy C276 (UNS N10276) is the industry standard for aggressive environments, exceptionally resistant to wet chlorine gas, hypochlorites, and chlorine dioxide. Hastelloy C22 (UNS N06022) offers better overall corrosion resistance than C276 in oxidizing environments with superior protection against localized corrosion, frequently used in pharmaceutical and biotech vessel fabrication. Hastelloy C2000 (UNS N06200) is a unique alloy with deliberate copper additions, providing maximum versatility in both oxidizing and reducing environments, excelling specifically in sulfuric acid service. Hastelloy C59, C4, and C-4 are specialized grades optimized for thermal stability and resistance to grain-boundary precipitation. Hastelloy B2 (UNS N10665) is a nickel-molybdenum alloy with significant resistance to hydrochloric acid at all concentrations and temperatures. Hastelloy B3 (UNS N10675) is an improved version of B2 with significantly enhanced thermal stability, making fabrication and welding of heavy sheets easier while maintaining the same high level of resistance to reducing acids. Hastelloy N (UNS N10003), also known as Alloy N, was developed specifically for service in molten fluoride salts.",

