    shortDescription:
      "Premium SMO 254 (UNS S31254 / F44) 6% Molybdenum super-austenitic plates and Alloy 20 (UNS N08020 / Carpenter 20) plates engineered for extreme corrosion resistance in halide environments and sulfuric acid applications. Manufactured to ASTM A240, ASME SA240, ASTM B463, and ASME SB463 standards.",

    technicalOverview:
      "SMO 254 is a 6% Molybdenum super-austenitic stainless steel specifically developed for use in halide-containing environments, such as brackish water, seawater, and pulp mill bleach plants. With a PREN (Pitting Resistance Equivalent Number) of > 42.5, it offers extraordinary resistance to localized attack. It provides significantly higher yield strength than standard austenitic steels, allowing for thinner plate designs in high-pressure systems. Key applications include desalination equipment, offshore oil and gas seawater systems, and flue-gas desulfurization (FGD) scrubbers. Alloy 20, often referred to as 'Carpenter 20,' is a 'super' stainless steel designed specifically for maximum resistance to acid attack. It effectively bridges the performance gap between stainless steel and expensive nickel-based alloys. It is renowned for its exceptional performance in hot sulfuric acid, particularly in concentrations of 20% to 40%. The addition of Niobium prevents intergranular corrosion by stabilizing the material against carbide precipitation during welding or thermal processing. Key applications include chemical production of synthetic fibers, explosives, plastics, and pharmaceutical mixing tanks.",

