      "Premium Monel 400 (UNS N04400 / 2.4360) nickel-copper alloy plates engineered for demanding marine and chemical environments, offering high strength and toughness over a wide temperature range with excellent resistance to seawater, hydrofluoric acid, and caustic alkalis. Manufactured to ASTM B127 and ASME SB127 standards.",

    technicalOverview:
      "Monel 400 is composed of approximately 63% Nickel and 30% Copper, providing a versatile material that bridges the gap between basic stainless steels and expensive highly-alloyed superalloys. It is the industry standard for marine engineering, exhibiting excellent resistance to rapidly flowing seawater and virtual immunity to chloride-ion stress corrosion cracking. It offers outstanding resistance to hydrofluoric acid in all concentrations up to the boiling point and is highly resistant to sulfuric and hydrochloric acids under reducing conditions. Monel 400 is famously resistant to alkalis (caustic soda) and maintains excellent mechanical properties from sub-zero temperatures up to 1000°F (538°C). The alloy can only be hardened by cold working, offering high strength and toughness over a wide temperature range.",

