  image: "/stock/inconel-plates.jpg",
  title: "Inconel Plates Supplier – 600, 601, 625, 690, 718, 725 & X-750",
  shortDescription: "Premium Inconel plates in grades 600, 601, 625, 690, 718, 725, and X-750. High-performance nickel-chromium-based superalloys engineered for extreme thermal and corrosive environments, maintaining exceptional tensile strength and structural integrity at high temperatures. Manufactured to ASTM B168, B443, B670 and ASME SB168 standards.",
  
  technicalOverview: "Inconel plates are a family of high-performance nickel-chromium-based superalloys engineered for the most extreme thermal and corrosive environments. These plates are characterized by their ability to maintain exceptional tensile strength and structural integrity at temperatures where standard stainless steels would undergo significant creep or oxidation. When exposed to high heat, Inconel forms a stable, passivating oxide layer that protects the plate surface from further environmental attack, making them indispensable for aerospace, nuclear, and high-pressure chemical processing. Inconel 600 (UNS N06600) offers superior resistance to chloride-ion stress corrosion cracking and alkaline solutions, performing reliably from cryogenic temperatures up to 2000°F (1093°C). Inconel 601 (UNS N06601) features additional aluminum content for enhanced resistance to high-temperature oxidation and spalling. Inconel 690 (UNS N06690) is engineered with high chromium content for excellent resistance to oxidizing acids and salts, making it the primary choice for nuclear steam generator components. Inconel 625 (UNS N06625) derives its high strength and fatigue resistance from molybdenum and niobium addition, ideal for offshore hardware and marine exhaust systems. Inconel 725 (UNS N07725) is an age-hardenable version of Alloy 625 providing nearly double the mechanical strength. Inconel 718 (UNS N07718) is renowned for its excellent weldability and resistance to post-weld cracking, essential for structural aerospace plates and cryogenic storage. Inconel X-750 (UNS N07750) is optimized for high-temperature structural components requiring minimal relaxation and high creep-rupture strength.",

  materialGroup: "Nickel-Chromium Superalloys",
  standards: "ASTM B168 / ASME SB168, API Dimensions, NACE MR 0175",
  forms: "Hot Rolled (HR), Cold Rolled (CR), Precision Cut",

