      "Inconel 601": "UNS N06601 (2.4851) – Features additional aluminum content providing enhanced resistance to high-temperature oxidation and spalling, even under severely cyclic heating conditions.",
      "Inconel 625": "UNS N06625 (2.4856) – Derives high strength and fatigue resistance from molybdenum and niobium addition. Highly resistant to pitting and crevice corrosion in seawater and chloride-heavy process streams.",
      "Inconel 690": "UNS N06690 (2.4642) – Engineered with high chromium content for excellent resistance to oxidizing acids and salts. Primary choice for nuclear steam generator components and high-temperature furnace liners.",
      "Inconel 718": "UNS N07718 (2.4668) – High-strength, corrosion-resistant alloy used from -423°F to 1300°F. Renowned for excellent weldability and resistance to post-weld cracking, essential for structural aerospace plates.",
