  image: "/stock/hastelloy-plates.jpg",
  title: "Hastelloy Plates Supplier – C22, C276, B2, B3, C2000, C59, C4 & HN",
  shortDescription: "Premium Hastelloy plates in grades C276, C22, B2, B3, C2000, C59, C4, and Alloy HN. High-performance nickel-molybdenum-chromium superalloys engineered to withstand the most aggressive chemical environments, offering exceptional resistance to pitting, stress-corrosion cracking, and a wide range of volatile chemical media. Manufactured to ASTM B575, B333 and ASME SB575, SB333 standards.",
  
  technicalOverview: "Hastelloy plates are high-performance nickel-molybdenum-chromium superalloys engineered to withstand the most aggressive chemical environments. These plates maintain exceptional mechanical integrity and corrosion resistance where standard stainless steels fail. They are particularly valued for their resistance to pitting, stress-corrosion cracking, and a wide range of volatile chemical media, including both oxidizing and reducing acids. Hastelloy C276 (UNS N10276) is the industry standard for aggressive environments, exceptionally resistant to wet chlorine gas, hypochlorites, and chlorine dioxide. Hastelloy C22 (UNS N06022) offers better overall corrosion resistance than C276 in oxidizing environments with superior protection against localized corrosion. Hastelloy C2000 (UNS N06200) is a unique alloy with deliberate copper additions, providing maximum versatility in both oxidizing and reducing environments, excelling specifically in sulfuric acid service. Hastelloy C59, C4, and C-4 are specialized grades optimized for thermal stability and resistance to grain-boundary precipitation. Hastelloy B2 (UNS N10665) is a nickel-molybdenum alloy with significant resistance to hydrochloric acid at all concentrations and temperatures. Hastelloy B3 (UNS N10675) is an improved version of B2 with significantly enhanced thermal stability, making fabrication and welding of heavy plates easier while maintaining the same high level of resistance to reducing acids.",

  materialGroup: "Nickel-Molybdenum-Chromium Superalloys",
  standards: "ASTM B575 / B333, ASME SB575 / SB333",
