      "Hastelloy C22": "UNS N06022 (2.4602) – Offers better overall corrosion resistance than C276 in oxidizing environments. Superior protection against localized corrosion. Frequently used in pharmaceutical and biotech vessel fabrication.",
      "Hastelloy B2": "UNS N10665 (2.4617) – Nickel-molybdenum alloy with significant resistance to hydrochloric acid at all concentrations and temperatures. Performs well in pure sulfuric and phosphoric acids.",
      "Hastelloy B3": "UNS N10675 (2.4600) – Improved version of B2 with significantly enhanced thermal stability. Easier fabrication and welding while maintaining high resistance to reducing acids.",
      "Hastelloy C2000": "UNS N06200 (2.4675) – Unique alloy with deliberate copper additions providing maximum versatility in both oxidizing and reducing environments. Excels specifically in sulfuric acid service.",
