      "High-alloy austenitic stainless steel pipes designed for maximum resistance to pitting and crevice corrosion. Features 6% Molybdenum content with a PREN of ≥42.5. Manufactured to ASTM A312, A358 and ASME SA312, SA358 standards.",

    // --- Complete Technical Data ---
    technicalOverview:
      "SMO 254, also known by the designation UNS S31254 and Werkstoff Number 1.4547, is a high-alloy austenitic stainless steel designed for maximum resistance to pitting and crevice corrosion. It is often referred to as a '6% Moly' grade due to its high molybdenum content. The chemical composition is a sophisticated balance of chromium (20%), nickel (18%), and molybdenum (6%), further enhanced with nitrogen and copper. The addition of nitrogen increases the yield strength and enhances the pitting resistance, while copper improves resistance to non-oxidizing acids like sulfuric and phosphoric acids. The metallurgical structure of SMO 254 pipes remains stable and austenitic, providing excellent ductility and impact strength even at sub-zero temperatures. Due to its high alloy content, it is significantly stronger than common 300-series stainless steels. This allows engineers to design piping systems with thinner walls without compromising structural integrity or pressure ratings, making it a cost-effective alternative to high-nickel alloys in many chloride-rich environments.",

    corrosionResistance: {
      pittingAndCrevice:
        "Exceptional resistance to localized corrosion in high-chloride environments with a PREN of ≥42.5. Specifically engineered to resist pitting and crevice corrosion in seawater and other aggressive halide solutions. Virtually immune to chloride-induced stress corrosion cracking.",
      chemicalMedia:
        "Robust resistance to a wide range of chemical media, including bleaching solutions used in the pulp and paper industry and aggressive reagents in chemical processing. The protective passive film formed on the surface is highly stable and reforms quickly if damaged, ensuring long-term structural efficiency and minimal maintenance requirements.",
      marineDurability:
        "Superior resistance to chlorides and acidic media, making it essential for offshore oil and gas seawater cooling systems, ballast water pipes, firewater systems, and desalination plants handling high-concentration brine.",
    },

