      "Incoloy 800H (UNS N08810) and Incoloy 800HT (UNS N08811) are high-performance nickel-iron-chromium alloys derived from the standard Incoloy 800 base. These pipes are designed to maintain a stable austenitic structure, providing exceptional resistance to oxidation, sulfidation, and carburization. The standout feature of Incoloy 800H and 800HT pipes is their superior mechanical strength at extreme temperatures. Raymond Ispat India is a premier manufacturer, supplier, and exporter of high-grade Incoloy 800H and 800HT Pipes in Mumbai, engineered for superior performance in high-temperature applications requiring creep-rupture strength. While both grades offer exceptional durability, the Incoloy 800HT (UNS N08811) variant is specially formulated with controlled composition for improved creep-rupture properties at elevated temperatures, making it the preferred choice for heavy-gauge components and complex fabrications.",

