    technicalOverview:
      "Hastelloy C276, technically classified under specifications such as ASTM B622 or UNS N10276, is one of the most versatile corrosion-resistant alloys available today. As a nickel-chromium-molybdenum-tungsten alloy, it is specifically designed to perform in a wide range of aggressive chemical environments. The material offers exceptional resistance to a broad spectrum of corrosive media, including wet chlorine gas and strong oxidizing agents like ferric and cupric chlorides. The primary advantage of Hastelloy C276 pipes is their outstanding reliability in both oxidizing and reducing environments. The alloy's unique composition provides exceptional resistance to pitting, crevice corrosion, and stress corrosion cracking, making it a reliable choice for the most demanding chemical processing applications.",

