    technicalOverview:
      "Super Duplex UNS S32760 pipes, also frequently referred to as F55, are high-performance industrial components manufactured for the most demanding environments. These pipes are specifically engineered to function effectively in aggressive chloride-containing surroundings where standard metals would quickly degrade. What sets the UNS S32760 composition apart from other duplex grades is the strategic addition of tungsten and copper, which significantly enhances its resistance to localized corrosion. As a core member of the super duplex category, this material perfectly balances the characteristics of both ferritic and austenitic steels. By maintaining this dual-phase structure, the pipes inherit the high mechanical strength of ferritic steel while benefiting from the exceptional corrosion resistance of austenitic steel. This hybrid nature makes UNS S32760 pipes widely applicable across a variety of critical industrial sectors. The superior performance of UNS S32760 pipes is rooted in a complex element combination that includes chromium, nickel, molybdenum, nitrogen, copper, and tungsten. This highly alloyed mixture ensures the pipes can withstand almost any working environment. The presence of these elements allows the material to achieve a higher yield strength than standard stainless steel grades while maintaining the durable corrosion-resistant properties of the austenitic phase. This makes them ideal for high-pressure systems that require long-term structural integrity.",

