      "Premium Copper Nickel 90/10 (UNS C70600 / 2.0872) pipes engineered with 9% to 11% nickel and controlled iron additions for superior corrosion resistance and biofouling protection in marine environments. Manufactured to ASTM B466, B467 and ASME SB466, SB467 standards.",

    technicalOverview:
      "RCM Metal & Alloy provides a complete range of high-performance Copper Nickel Alloy 90/10 Pipes, including seamless and welded configurations, at a competitive price point. Grade 90/10 (UNS C70600) is an established engineering material composed primarily of copper and nickel, with controlled additions of iron and manganese to enhance its structural integrity. This specific alloy is a staple in the Mumbai industrial market due to its consistency and reliability in conveying substances across complex piping networks. The chemical composition of our Cu-Ni 90/10 pipes is meticulously balanced, featuring 9% to 11% nickel and a base of copper. Significant trace elements include iron (1% to 1.8%) for improved erosion resistance, along with controlled maximums of manganese, carbon, zinc, and phosphorus. One of the most notable attributes of UNS C70600 pipes is their superior resistance to biofouling. The applications for 90/10 Cupro Nickel pipes are extensive, particularly in offshore and marine sectors where they are used for saltwater pipes, fittings, valves, and pump components.",

