    shortDescription:
      "Premium Stainless Steel 321 (UNS S32100 / 1.4541) titanium-stabilized austenitic pipes engineered for high-heat environments, offering remarkable resistance to intergranular corrosion and creep at temperatures from 800°F to 1500°F. Manufactured to ASTM A312, A358 and ASME SA312, SA358 standards.",

    technicalOverview:
      "RCM Metal & Alloy is a specialized manufacturer, supplier, and importer of high-performance Stainless Steel 321 Pipes in Mumbai, specifically engineered for high-heat environments where stabilization is critical. Grade 321 (UNS S32100) is an austenitic stainless steel uniquely alloyed with Titanium, which provides remarkable resistance to intergranular corrosion during chromium carbide precipitation. This makes it superior for continuous service at temperatures ranging from 800°F to 1500°F (427°C to 816°C). Unlike other grades, SS 321 is developed to increase creep resistance and structural stability, ensuring it remains robust under stress ruptures and high-pressure conditions. Our product range includes Jindal SS 321 Pipes, available in seamless, welded, ERW, square, and rectangular profiles. These pipes are identified for their ability to resist polythionic acid stress corrosion cracking, especially in hydrocarbon and refinery applications. While SS 321 cannot be hardened by heat treatment, it excels in formability through cold working and can be properly welded using standard shop fabrication procedures. With a high density and oxidation resistance up to 1600°F, these pipes are ideal for chloride-free caustic solutions and low-temperature services, offering a versatile balance of tensile and yield stress characteristics.",

