    shortDescription:
      "Premium Stainless Steel 317L (UNS S31703 / 1.4438) low-carbon, molybdenum-bearing austenitic pipes engineered for environments where standard 316L grades fall short, offering significantly enhanced resistance to chemical attack in acidic, chloride, and brine solutions. Manufactured to ASTM A312, A358 and ASME SA312, SA358 standards.",

    technicalOverview:
      "Raymond Ispat India is a premier manufacturer and global exporter of high-performance Stainless Steel 317L Pipes in Mumbai, specifically engineered for environments where standard 316L grades fall short. As a low-carbon, molybdenum-bearing austenitic alloy, Grade 317L (UNS S31703 / 1.4438) offers significantly enhanced resistance to chemical attack, particularly in acidic, chloride, and brine solutions. This unique chemical composition—enriched with higher levels of chromium, nickel, and nitrogen—enables the construction of thinner-walled pipes without compromising structural integrity, effectively reducing material weight while maximizing durability in harsh automotive, textile, and wastewater processing settings. Our product inventory includes Jindal SS 317L Pipes, available in seamless, welded, ERW, and EFW configurations across round, square, and custom profiles. Compliant with ASME SA312 TP317L and international standards, these pipes boast exceptional formability and weldability, shielding against intergranular corrosion during fabrication. Their impressive thermal stability and high-pressure resilience make them indispensable for flue gas desulfurization, petrochemical plants, and heat-related applications.",

