  technicalOverview: "SMO 254 is a high-end austenitic stainless steel with high molybdenum and nitrogen content, specifically developed for use in halide-containing environments such as seawater, brackish water, and pulp mill bleach plants. With a PREN (Pitting Resistance Equivalent Number) of > 42.5, these tubes offer resistance to pitting and crevice corrosion that far exceeds Grade 316L. Due to nitrogen alloying, SMO 254 has significantly higher yield strength than conventional austenitic steels while maintaining excellent ductility and impact strength. It provides exceptional performance in high-chloride process streams and acidic solutions where localized attack is a primary concern. Alloy 20 is a 'super' austenitic stainless steel designed for maximum resistance to acid attack, specifically sulfuric acid. It offers extraordinary resistance to hot sulfuric acid (H₂SO₄) at concentrations up to 95%. The addition of copper is the key factor in protecting the metal against this specific reducing acid. Alloy 20 is stabilized with Columbium (Niobium) to minimize carbide precipitation during welding, ensuring the heat-affected zone remains corrosion-resistant. It provides excellent resistance to intergranular corrosion and chloride-ion stress corrosion cracking.",

