  shortDescription: "Premium Monel 400 (UNS N04400 / 2.4360) nickel-copper alloy tubes engineered for exceptional resistance to seawater, hydrofluoric acid, sulfuric acid, and alkalies. Ideal for marine engineering, chemical processing, and heat exchanger applications. Manufactured to ASTM B163, B165, B725, B730 and ASME SB163, SB165 standards.",
  
  technicalOverview: "Monel 400 tubes (UNS N04400) are high-performance nickel-copper alloy piping solutions renowned for their exceptional resistance to seawater, hydrofluoric acid, sulfuric acid, and alkalies. This solid-solution alloy provides a unique combination of high strength, excellent weldability, and toughness across a wide temperature range, from cryogenic levels up to 538°C (1000°F). Monel 400 offers exceptional resistance to rapidly flowing seawater and does not suffer from significant pitting or crevice corrosion in marine environments, making it ideal for splash zone applications. It is one of the few materials that can handle hydrofluoric acid (HF) in all concentrations up to the boiling point. It also offers excellent resistance to non-oxidizing acids like H₂SO₄ and H₃PO₄. It maintains excellent mechanical properties at sub-zero temperatures and does not undergo a ductile-to-brittle transition even at the temperature of liquid hydrogen, ensuring structural safety in cryogenic gas handling. In many marine applications, Monel 400 exhibits natural resistance to the attachment of barnacles and algae, maintaining flow efficiency in intake systems.",

